    text:"Andreessen Horowitz launched the Machine Age Fund with $1.1 billion to invest in AI infrastructure startups building chips, memory, networking, systems software, and power infrastructure specifically for training and running frontier AI models. The fund targets founders building 'the stack below the models' -- positioning infrastructure as the binding constraint as frontier labs' capex requirements continue accelerating.",
